WEBVTT

NOTE
Journey: Advocates — Week 15 Leader Video
Unit 4, Lesson 3: Agency

1
00:00:06.060 --> 00:00:08.740
The ability to choose.

2
00:00:09.820 --> 00:00:13.180
In fact, so many questions about why things happen

3
00:00:13.180 --> 00:00:16.740
are answered with just simply humanity's ability

4
00:00:16.740 --> 00:00:18.700
to make a choice.

5
00:00:18.700 --> 00:00:22.220
And choices really are what governs so much of our lives

6
00:00:22.220 --> 00:00:26.340
from the easiest decisions to some of the hardest

7
00:00:26.340 --> 00:00:29.500
to choices that take forever to make

8
00:00:29.500 --> 00:00:32.100
and ones that we make in an instant.

9
00:00:32.100 --> 00:00:36.060
And it's choices that are so powerful

10
00:00:36.060 --> 00:00:39.020
and they're a privilege and they're a responsibility

11
00:00:39.020 --> 00:00:41.620
and it's something that God has given us.

12
00:00:41.620 --> 00:00:43.260
And this is one of those, again,

13
00:00:43.260 --> 00:00:46.660
one of those pointers to who God is

14
00:00:46.660 --> 00:00:48.620
and the fact that he exists.

15
00:00:48.620 --> 00:00:50.740
But here's the key question.

16
00:00:50.740 --> 00:00:53.660
How do students' choices,

17
00:00:53.660 --> 00:00:57.900
how do all of our choices actually reflect God?

18
00:00:57.900 --> 00:00:59.780
How do the things that we choose,

19
00:00:59.780 --> 00:01:02.220
whether it be right, whether it be wrong, good, bad,

20
00:01:02.220 --> 00:01:04.340
ugly, whatever it is,

21
00:01:04.340 --> 00:01:07.540
how do those choices reflect God?

22
00:01:07.540 --> 00:01:10.020
Some of our choices obviously do.

23
00:01:10.020 --> 00:01:13.180
A lot of our choices obviously don't.

24
00:01:13.180 --> 00:01:15.180
But when we talk about our ability to choose

25
00:01:15.180 --> 00:01:17.980
and the fact that God gave it to us,

26
00:01:17.980 --> 00:01:19.580
there's some things we really have to make sure

27
00:01:19.580 --> 00:01:21.340
we nail down with our students.

28
00:01:21.340 --> 00:01:24.260
So we're challenging students with two things.

29
00:01:24.260 --> 00:01:29.060
Number one, that our free will points us to him.

30
00:01:29.100 --> 00:01:31.300
The fact that we have free will

31
00:01:31.300 --> 00:01:33.180
is a pointer to who he is.

32
00:01:33.180 --> 00:01:35.980
It helps us understand that because we have the ability

33
00:01:35.980 --> 00:01:38.980
to choose that God is out there somewhere.

34
00:01:38.980 --> 00:01:42.900
But number two, our free will should reflect him

35
00:01:43.820 --> 00:01:46.660
and how we behave as Christians

36
00:01:46.660 --> 00:01:49.540
ought to be a reflection of who he is.

37
00:01:49.540 --> 00:01:51.660
So as you go about your unit this week,

38
00:01:51.660 --> 00:01:53.300
I want you to keep something in mind.

39
00:01:53.300 --> 00:01:54.140
I want you to take,

40
00:01:54.140 --> 00:01:56.300
last week we took a temperature of our students

41
00:01:56.300 --> 00:01:58.980
to figure out where the students are.

42
00:01:58.980 --> 00:02:02.940
This week I want you to take temperature of your community.

43
00:02:02.940 --> 00:02:04.340
Now we talked at the very beginning

44
00:02:04.340 --> 00:02:06.820
about the importance of establishing a community,

45
00:02:06.820 --> 00:02:09.180
a strong community, a community that is open,

46
00:02:09.180 --> 00:02:11.180
one that loves, one that's close,

47
00:02:11.180 --> 00:02:12.820
one that students feel safe in.

48
00:02:12.820 --> 00:02:15.580
We talked about that kind of being an overarching goal

49
00:02:15.580 --> 00:02:18.260
of being able to communicate truth and love

50
00:02:18.260 --> 00:02:19.940
is to have a community where students feel safe

51
00:02:19.940 --> 00:02:22.780
to ask questions and so forth.

52
00:02:22.780 --> 00:02:24.700
So how is that community doing?

53
00:02:24.700 --> 00:02:26.740
How is it working?

54
00:02:26.740 --> 00:02:28.460
Are there adjustments that you need to make?

55
00:02:28.460 --> 00:02:32.420
It's so easy, especially as a leader of large groups

56
00:02:32.420 --> 00:02:35.340
to figure out, okay, how are all these groups working?

57
00:02:35.340 --> 00:02:36.780
Is there other issues?

58
00:02:36.780 --> 00:02:37.940
Are there not?

59
00:02:37.940 --> 00:02:40.220
Does everybody feel that they belong?

60
00:02:40.220 --> 00:02:42.220
Even if you only do a small group yourself,

61
00:02:42.220 --> 00:02:45.300
it's really easy to get caught up and forget

62
00:02:45.300 --> 00:02:47.020
about maybe one particular student

63
00:02:47.020 --> 00:02:50.260
that has a ton of really great things to say.

64
00:02:50.260 --> 00:02:51.500
But for some reason,

65
00:02:51.500 --> 00:02:54.060
doesn't feel like they can say those things.

66
00:02:54.060 --> 00:02:56.100
So it's good to take a step back,

67
00:02:56.100 --> 00:02:57.620
take a look at our communities

68
00:02:57.620 --> 00:03:00.900
and see are we hitting the mark, but where we wanna be.

69
00:03:00.900 --> 00:03:02.980
So a couple of things I want you to think about.

70
00:03:02.980 --> 00:03:05.300
Are leaders providing the right atmosphere?

71
00:03:06.180 --> 00:03:09.780
Are they crafting that sort of atmosphere of discussion?

72
00:03:09.780 --> 00:03:11.180
One that questions our welcome,

73
00:03:11.180 --> 00:03:14.300
one of grace and love, but with truth

74
00:03:14.300 --> 00:03:16.300
and not letting one student dominate,

75
00:03:16.300 --> 00:03:18.500
inviting all students to participate.

76
00:03:18.500 --> 00:03:20.740
All of those pieces of the puzzle

77
00:03:20.740 --> 00:03:24.100
is the right kind of atmosphere being fostered.

78
00:03:24.100 --> 00:03:27.300
Number two, are students being loved?

79
00:03:27.300 --> 00:03:30.340
And are they being challenged?

80
00:03:30.340 --> 00:03:32.460
So often we kind of confuse the two

81
00:03:32.460 --> 00:03:34.180
and we think that for loving students

82
00:03:34.180 --> 00:03:35.260
and we're just kind of letting them think

83
00:03:35.260 --> 00:03:37.140
what they wanna think and we're,

84
00:03:37.140 --> 00:03:42.140
in my experience, the most challenged students that I had

85
00:03:42.700 --> 00:03:45.900
in terms of how much I challenged them

86
00:03:45.900 --> 00:03:47.940
were the ones that felt most loved

87
00:03:47.940 --> 00:03:49.340
at the end of a year.

88
00:03:49.340 --> 00:03:54.220
Those are the ones that felt like they were valued.

89
00:03:54.380 --> 00:03:57.860
Go to any school, in any classroom,

90
00:03:57.860 --> 00:04:01.380
where in the middle of things, students are frustrated,

91
00:04:01.380 --> 00:04:05.900
they're under pressure, and they think a teacher

92
00:04:05.900 --> 00:04:07.860
or somebody is really too hard on them

93
00:04:07.860 --> 00:04:10.180
and they complain about it.

94
00:04:10.180 --> 00:04:12.900
If you notice, go back to those schools

95
00:04:12.900 --> 00:04:15.300
and ask those teachers how many graduates

96
00:04:15.300 --> 00:04:16.540
come back to see them.

97
00:04:17.540 --> 00:04:19.420
And the number's probably pretty high.

98
00:04:20.380 --> 00:04:23.580
The more, sort of works this way,

99
00:04:23.620 --> 00:04:26.620
the more challenging you are with the student,

100
00:04:26.620 --> 00:04:28.860
the greater respect you gain

101
00:04:28.860 --> 00:04:32.220
and the greater love that you are showing them.

102
00:04:32.220 --> 00:04:33.500
It just works that way.

103
00:04:33.500 --> 00:04:34.860
So make sure that you love them

104
00:04:34.860 --> 00:04:37.260
but make sure that you also challenge them.

105
00:04:37.260 --> 00:04:41.180
Number three, do they feel safe to be honest?

106
00:04:41.180 --> 00:04:42.620
I mean, if we're loving them properly,

107
00:04:42.620 --> 00:04:43.980
then that's probably gonna be the case

108
00:04:43.980 --> 00:04:45.340
that they do feel safe.

109
00:04:45.340 --> 00:04:47.180
But there are some things that we want students

110
00:04:47.180 --> 00:04:51.380
to be honest but sometimes their honesty

111
00:04:51.380 --> 00:04:53.100
causes us to have to react in a way

112
00:04:53.100 --> 00:04:54.980
that they don't want us to react.

113
00:04:54.980 --> 00:04:56.300
But do they feel safe?

114
00:04:56.300 --> 00:04:58.220
Do they feel like they can be honest with us

115
00:04:58.220 --> 00:05:01.020
and then we're gonna react appropriately?

116
00:05:01.020 --> 00:05:06.020
Number four, are your small groups serving one another?

117
00:05:06.420 --> 00:05:09.220
Are you guys in your small groups caring for one another?

118
00:05:09.220 --> 00:05:12.460
Have you created a community where you love each other

119
00:05:12.460 --> 00:05:14.060
or the students are loving on each other?

120
00:05:14.060 --> 00:05:16.780
It isn't just a place where you kind of come together,

121
00:05:16.780 --> 00:05:18.900
say a few things and then off you go

122
00:05:18.900 --> 00:05:21.020
into something else and off to your real friends

123
00:05:21.020 --> 00:05:22.540
or whatever the case is.

124
00:05:23.300 --> 00:05:26.620
Are your small groups becoming a tight knit community

125
00:05:26.620 --> 00:05:29.220
of people who care and love for one another?

126
00:05:29.220 --> 00:05:32.140
And I would encourage you as a next step for that

127
00:05:32.140 --> 00:05:34.180
is to take those and get those students out

128
00:05:34.180 --> 00:05:36.620
into the community whether it be the wider community

129
00:05:36.620 --> 00:05:37.900
or even just the church community

130
00:05:37.900 --> 00:05:40.500
and find places for them to serve together

131
00:05:40.500 --> 00:05:42.500
and do things together to help build

132
00:05:42.500 --> 00:05:44.380
and foster that kind of community.

133
00:05:44.380 --> 00:05:46.260
All right, so you've almost made it

134
00:05:46.260 --> 00:05:47.780
to the halfway point.

135
00:05:47.780 --> 00:05:49.460
Congratulations, keep it up.

136
00:05:49.460 --> 00:05:52.380
You guys are doing a great job, I am sure.

137
00:05:52.380 --> 00:05:54.820
And remember, some of your students might be starting

138
00:05:54.820 --> 00:05:56.500
to feel some of the stress of school

139
00:05:56.500 --> 00:05:58.260
because you're probably getting around midterms

140
00:05:58.260 --> 00:06:00.300
and finals and tests and quizzes

141
00:06:00.300 --> 00:06:01.140
and those kinds of things.

142
00:06:01.140 --> 00:06:02.500
So now would be a really good time

143
00:06:02.500 --> 00:06:04.500
and this is a really good lesson

144
00:06:04.500 --> 00:06:07.460
to do some fun things, to have some fun

145
00:06:07.460 --> 00:06:09.780
with students on making choices,

146
00:06:09.780 --> 00:06:11.100
whether it be through games,

147
00:06:11.100 --> 00:06:13.660
whether it be through examples, something silly,

148
00:06:13.660 --> 00:06:15.620
where you could have a whole bunch of fun

149
00:06:15.620 --> 00:06:17.500
having students make choices

150
00:06:17.500 --> 00:06:18.660
but at the same time,

151
00:06:18.660 --> 00:06:20.780
teach them the power of those choices.

